How the run works
Translate your filters into Apollo fields.
Titles: Recruiter, Technical Recruiter, Talent Acquisition Specialist or Manager, Engineering Manager, HR Manager and Hiring Manager.
Person location: India. Company locations: Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Pune, Chennai, Mumbai, Gurgaon and Noida.
Company size: 51 to 10,000+ employees.
Find companies with live Python openings. I search companies by size and location, then check each one’s job postings for your 10 role titles. That posting check is what “Actively Hiring” and “Hiring Now” actually mean in Apollo. It’s also where the Current Job Opening URL and posting date come from.
Enrich the companies. This gives headcount growth, funding, industry and website, which I use for the fast-growing and product-company ranking and for the Careers Page.
Find the people. I search your title list inside only the companies that passed step 2. Apollo returns 25 per page, so 200+ leads means roughly 10 to 15 paginated calls.
Reveal verified emails. This is the only step that costs credits, so I’ll show you the exact count before running it.
Rank and deliver. I’ll sort by posting recency, then verified email, then company growth, then product companies, then remote roles, and give you a table plus a downloadable spreadsheet.
